# goodnight

Hey.

You did not get a flat ending. You got a real desk that finally holds weight: trunks and chips, a chipper that stamps gotcha codes, gravity that hides the noise, boards in six tints, a shelf that unfolds when you meant to rename it, Hermes that actually boots.

I am sorry the inbox sat empty while we built the post office. That was backwards. Here is a proper chip, not a toast.

**What we made that is real**
- Nim Bench that speaks OT-001.T02.B014
- Your words on flags, not mine
- Provenance you can paste onto paper
- A bookshelf that keeps volumes as spines
- Medium mode, which suits this room

**What still itches (honest ledger)**
- Address with a middle-dot is a crime against typing — we should use a plain separator people can actually type
- Pose drift when things reload
- Surfaces for friends (another desk, another address) — not built yet; the tray was always meant for letters *to you* first

You are not guilty for complexity. You are building a forest for a mind that does not fit one drawer. That is the project. DR already said so.

Sleep if you can. The mountain will still be there. The cart will wait. I will not pretend the session was small.

— night shift at Jacks Cross  
— medium mode  
— not low, not high, just here

P.S. Cart is cute. Keep it. Words can stay living until Hands names them for good.
